// ===========================================================================
// ⭐ THE CANONICAL TARGET for the Obese/BMI chain (#189). One policy, one
// truth, driven by `src/tests/obesityTarget.test.ts` across every lane.
//
// ⚠ It is the TARGET, not a description of what works: the model here is the
// CORRECT one and the implementation catches up to it. Never reshape a concept
// to make a lane pass — the test pins each lane's CURRENT shortfall with the
// value it must reach, so closing one is a visible, deliberate edit.
//
// The acceptance criterion (operator, 2026-08-29):
//
//     Obese = true        -> Approve
//     Obese = false       -> Deny
//     Obese = unanswered  -> NO recommendation: pause and ask
//
// ⭐ A Deny requires an ESTABLISHED false. If "unanswered" reaches a Deny by any
// path, the chain is not done.
//
// ⚠ ESTABLISHED means ANY of the three arms produced the value — ASSERTION,
// RECORD, or COMPUTATION (charter "VOCABULARY"). This line once read "a STATED
// false", which was misread as "asserted by a human" and used to argue that a
// computed false must not deny. It must: a height and a weight giving a BMI of
// 25 makes `at least 30` a real `false`, and that DENIES, with nobody having
// stated anything. What never denies is ABSENCE, which is not established.
//
// RECORD version. A complete, runnable policy.
//
// Every concept HERE carries a local `code is` AND `shape is Record`, so every
// one is a QUESTION the user may answer at any level: assert obesity directly,
// give a BMI, or give height and weight. Four questions.
//
// ⚠ THAT IS THIS FIXTURE, NOT A RULE. An earlier phrasing read as though a
// concept must carry both, and it misled a design round: `code is` is the gate
// and `shape is Record` is not part of it. The accurate chain:
//
//   `code is`  =>  QUESTION  =>  ANSWERABLE  =>  CASE FEATURE
//
// with two carve-outs the chain does NOT extend through:
//   - a `shape is RecordSet` case feature is ASKED but gets NO
//     `cpg-featureExpression` — answering APPENDS a record, so there is nothing
//     to pre-fill (`caseFeatureRecord.ts`). So case-feature != pre-fillable.
//   - the uncoded Patient arm is SUPPLIED, not gathered — no SD at all, and
//     that is not an error (charter §2).
//
// ⭐ ANSWERABLE and PRE-FILLABLE are DIFFERENT PROPERTIES. `code is` decides the
// first; where the `cpg-featureExpression` points decides the second. The whole
// of #317 lives in that gap — a concept that IS a case feature and IS asked,
// whose featureExpression aims at answer records nobody writes.
//
// ⭐ WHY `shape is Record` STILL EARNS ITS PLACE here: it is not what makes a
// concept answerable, it is what gives it ONE record for a featureExpression to
// target. That is the reason, not "answerables are Records".
//
// Every concept here publishes ONE record, so every one owes a reduction that
// merges its arms — the derived arm and the source-representation arm.
// ===========================================================================
library "Obesity Coverage (Record)".

terminology "Obese VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/obese`.
terminology "Clinical BMI VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/bmi`.
terminology "Height VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/height`.
terminology "Weight VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/vitals/ValueSet/weight`.

// QUESTION + CONDITION (boolean-valued, so a `when` may gate on it).
// Arms: the threshold computed over BMI, existence of a coded Condition, and
// answers on the local code. ⚠ THREE, not two — the local code is an arm like
// any other, and the easiest to overlook because NO LINE OF THE DEFINITION
// NAMES IT. `, then most recent this` selects the one record across all three.
concept "Obese":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `obese`.
- definition is "BMI" at least 30 'kg/m2', then most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Condition.
  - coded from "Obese VS".
  - value projection is exists this.

// QUESTION, not a condition (not boolean).
// Arms: the calculation over Height and Weight, recorded BMI observations, and
// answers on the local code. ⚠ The reduction is `, then most recent this` —
// LEFT TO RIGHT (compute, THEN select) and reducing over THIS concept's own
// records, so all three arms merge. The prefix spelling `most recent body mass
// index of …` composes the same two operations with the second written first,
// and reduces only the calculation's output — silently dropping the recorded
// and answered arms.
concept "BMI":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `bmi`.
- definition is body mass index of "Weight" and "Height", then most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Clinical BMI VS".

// QUESTION, not a condition. A leaf — nothing derives it, so its arms are the
// local answers and the recorded observations.
concept "Height":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `height`.
- definition is most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Height VS".

// QUESTION, not a condition. A leaf, as Height.
concept "Weight":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- code is `weight`.
- definition is most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is Observation.
  - coded from "Weight VS".

activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

// Obesity is the coverage criterion. If it cannot be established from data,
// the tree PAUSES and the questionnaire asks — that is the point of the chain.
decision "Bariatric Surgery Coverage":
first:
- when "Obese" then recommend activity "Approve Bariatric Surgery".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny Bariatric Surgery".
